UID:17043
DTSTART;TZID=America/Chicago:20261203T120000
SEQUENCE:0
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
DTEND;TZID=America/Chicago:20261203T130000
LOCATION:4580 Scott Ave\, St. Louis\, MO\, United States
SUMMARY:Oliver/Lenihan/Hicks Trio at the Med Campus
CLASS:PUBLIC
DESCRIPTION:The trio of Oliver\, Lenihan\, Hicks will perform a set of jazz
 \nstandards based in the traditions of the Great American Songbook\,\nbebo
 p\, and modern jazz\, including music by Miles Davis\, Bill Evans\,\nJohn 
 Coltrane\, and Keith Jarrett. Pianist Jay Oliver's distinctive\,\nadventur
 ous approach to improvisation within the trio's interactivity\nbreathes li
 fe into the standard repertoire of jazz.\n\nOLIVER/LENIHAN/HICKS TRIO\n\nJ
 ay Oliver\, keyboards\nWilliam Lenihan\, guitar\, bass\nDemarius Hicks\, p
 ercussion\n\nLOCATION/PARKING\n\nThe best entrance to access Moore Auditor
 ium is through the Farrell\nLearning and Teaching Center\, 522 Euclid Ave\
 , St Louis\, MO\, 63110. MAP\n[https://www.google.com/maps/place/522+Eucli
 d+Ave\,+St.+Louis\,+MO+63110/@38.635374\,-90.2655604\,841m/data=!3m2!1e3!4
 b1!4m5!3m4!1s0x87d8b52094bda175:0x6bb584b2b573c1e8!8m2!3d38.635374!4d-90.2
 629855?entry=ttu&amp;g_ep=EgoyMDI1MTExNy4wIKXMDSoASAFQAw%3D%3D]\n\nPlaza Garag
 e is the best place to park. 3 Barnes-Jewish Hospital\nPlaza\, St. Louis\,
  MO 63110. Map\n[https://www.google.com/maps/place/3+Barnes+Jewish+Hospita
 l+Plaza\,+St.+Louis\,+MO+63110/@38.6347008\,-90.26755\,841m/data=!3m2!1e3!
 4b1!4m6!3m5!1s0x87d8b5210f6bd195:0x720258c706995a60!8m2!3d38.6347008!4d-90
 .2649751!16s%2Fg%2F11cncj9kq4?entry=ttu&amp;g_ep=EgoyMDI1MTExNy4wIKXMDSoASAFQA
 w%3D%3D]\n\n-------------------------\n\nJAY OLIVER\n\nJay Oliver\, keyboa
 rds\, jazz and studio musician\, producer who for\ndecades based in both 
 New York and Los Angeles - performed and\nrecorded with jazz icons of the 
 industry including the famed Maynard\nFerguson Band\, Dave Weckl\, Chick C
 orea\, Mike Brecker\, Mike Stern and\nnumerous others. In the studio and t
 ouring worlds he has worked with\nBonnie Raitt\, Celine Dion\, Glenn Frey\
 , The Eagles\, legendary studio\ndrummer Russ Kunkel\, producer Jay Graydo
 n\, Sheryl Crow\, Jimmy Buffett\nand many others. \n\nWILLIAM LENIHAN\n\n
 William Lenihan\, guitar\, bass\, composer\, performer and producer who\nf
 or decades has performed\, recorded and toured with a wide array of\niconi
 c artists from jazz\, pop\, the theatre and film worlds to\nclassical musi
 c - including jazz legends Ron Carter\, Michael Brecker\,\nDave Weckl\, Ga
 ry Husband\, Marc Copland\, John Patitucci\, Bob Brookmeyer\nand many more
 . In the pop world he has worked with legends Petula\nClark\, Julie Andrew
 s\, Bernadette Peters\, The Shirelles\, Suzanne\nSomers\, Sheryl Crow and 
 dozens more. He also works in film music with\nnumerous credits including 
 music for George Lucas\, Ron Howard and has\nperformed as classical guitar
 ist and mandolinist with major symphony\,\nopera\, studio and theatre orch
 estras in New York\, Los Angeles\, St.\nLouis and Europe. He has collabora
 ted in concert with noted composers\nand performers such as Donald Erb\, A
 lexander Goehr\, Roberto\nFabricciani.\n\nDEMARIUS HICKS\n\nDemarius Hicks
  is a percussionist whose expressive creativity and\ngenre-spanning versat
 ility have made him one of the region’s most\ndynamic musical voices. A 
 native of East St. Louis\, Hicks brings a\nvibrant blend of gospel\, strai
 ght-ahead jazz\, funk\, fusion\,\nAfro-Cuban\, R&amp;B\, hip hop\, and more to
  every performance. Mentored by\nMarvin Sparks at the University of Missou
 ri–St. Louis\, Hicks honed\nhis craft with a deep respect for tradition 
 and a bold\, innovative\nspirit. He has performed on tour with artists suc
 h as Stefon Harris\,\nMarc Cary\, Nicholas Payton\, and Russell Gunn\, whi
 le also remaining a\nvital force in the St. Louis scene alongside locals D
 enise Thimes\,\nAnita Jackson\, Ptah Williams.\n
DTSTAMP:20261119T182346Z
END:VEVENT
