BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:17011
DTSTART;TZID=America/Chicago:20261120T155000
SEQUENCE:0
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
DTEND;TZID=America/Chicago:20261120T165000
LOCATION:560 Trinity Ave\, University City\, 63130
SUMMARY:Friends of Music Concerto &amp; Aria Competition
CLASS:PUBLIC
DESCRIPTION:Sponsored by Friends of Music (Join here!\n[https://music.washu
 .edu/our-music-community])\n\nThe Friends of Music Concerto &amp; Aria Competi
 tion is open to students\nof Washington University in St. Louis. The winne
 r will perform with\nthe Washington University Symphony Orchestra and will
  receive a\nFriends of Music $500 merit award.\n \n\nPERFORMERS\n\n_Fanta
 isie brillante sur_ \"Carmen\" (1880) by François Borne\n(1840–1920) 
    \n     Priya Ramotar\, Flute &amp; Matthew Mazzoni\, Piano\n\nFlute C
 oncerto by Otar Godefini (1928- 1994) \n     Lena Stern\, Flute &amp; Mat
 thew Mazzoni\, Piano\n\n_Serenade_ (1948) by Howard Hanson (1896–1981) 
    \n     Giulia Vitolo\, Flute &amp; Matthew Mazzoni\, Piano\n\nFlute C
 oncerto No. 2 in D Major\, K. 314 (1778) by W. A. Mozart\n(1756–1791) 
    \n     Jackson Liu\, Flute &amp; Matthew Mazzoni\, Piano\n\nViolin Co
 ncerto in E minor\, Movement 1 (1844) by Felix Mendelssohn\n(1809–1847)
  \n     Anthony He\, Violin &amp; Young Kim\, Piano\n\nViolin Concerto in 
 D minor\, Op. 47\, Mvt. 1 (1903) by Jean Sibelius\n(1865–1957) \n   
