SUMMARY:Her Light\, Her Line\, Her Song: Chamber Music at the St. Louis Art
 \nMuseum
CLASS:PUBLIC
DESCRIPTION:This concert features chamber music by Lili Boulanger\, Mélani
 e Bonis\,\nand Louise Farrenc for flute\, cello\, piano\, and voice. Inspi
 red by\nWomen Impressionists and the Land\, the program shines a light on 
 the\nImpressionist influences that extended beyond the canvas to women\nco
 mposers of the era—artists who broke boundaries\, defied\nexpectations\,
  and helped shape the musical landscape of their time.\n\nPROGRAM\n\n_Suit
 e Orientale_\, Op. 48 (1900) by Mélanie \"Mel\" Bonis (1858-1937) \nFrom
  _Clairières dans le ciel_ (1914) by Lili Boulanger (1893-1918)\n     
 No. 2. _Elle est gravement gaie_\n     No. 4. _Un poète disait_\n   
   No. 8. _Vous m'avez regardé avec toute votre âme_\n_Le retour _(1912)
  by Lili Boulanger \n_Octobre\,_ Op. 23 No. 1 (1932) by Charlotte Sohy (1
 887-1955)\nTrio\, Op. 45 (1862) by Louise Farrenc (1804-1875)\n\nWASHU FAC
 ULTY PERFORMERS\n\nJennifer Gartley\nKimberly Jeong\nErin Haupt\nYeon-Kyun
 g Kim\n
DTSTAMP:20261119T182346Z
END:VEVENT
