SUMMARY:St. Louis Symphony on the South 40
CLASS:PUBLIC
DESCRIPTION:This special collaboration will take place outside on the South
  40\n(near Bear's Den) on the beautiful Danforth Campus.  Members of the
 \nSt. Louis Symphony will perform following a WashU string\nensemble. Thi
 s event is free\, family-friendly\, and open to the\npublic! \n\nDirecti
 ons [https://wustl.edu/about/campuses/maps-directions-parking/]\nCampus Ma
 p [https://washu.edu/life-at-washu/getting-around/]\n(performance location
  outside Umrath House\, building #326\, map\nlocation C8)\nPublic Parking 
 Information\n[https://washu.edu/life-at-washu/getting-around/] (It is sug
 gested\nthat visitors park in the Danforth University Center parking garag
 e -\n#200\, map location E4 on the campus map.)\n\nIn case of inclement 
 weather\, the concert will take place inside Risa\nCommons just southeast 
 of the outdoor space.\n\nThis event is in cooperation with Student Transi
 tions &amp; Family\nPrograms\n\nWASHU STRING ENSEMBLE\n\nPROGRAM\n\n_Hornpipe_
  from _Water Music_ by Handel\n_Adagio Cantabile _from _Cinnamon Grove_ by
  Nathaniel Dett\n_Autumn_ from _The Four Seasons _by Vivaldi \n_Nine To F
 ive _by Dolly Parton \n\nENSEMBLE\n\nVIOLINS\nBrad Gober\nIan Lee\nMichel
 le Lee\nErin Suh\nJessica Hu\nSadie Navid\nAshley Hong\n\nVIOLA\nEmily Upd
 ike\nHannah An\nAnanyaa Srivatsan\n\nCELLO\nMax Zeller\nJackson Bai\nYoann
 a Choi\n\nBASS\nMichael Moore\n\nST. LOUIS SYMPHONY ENSEMBLE\n\n_Landscape
  _for Low Brass - “El Cholla Cha-Cha” by Gerry Pagano \n_Harmonic Tap
 estry_ for Low Brass_ _by Adrienne Albert  \nSuite for Bass Trombone and 
 Tuba by John Stevens \n“Ballade” from Trombone Quartet Memories by K
 ieko Takashima\nQuartet No. 1 - II. _Allegro_ &amp; IV. _Allegro_ by Anthony 
 Plog \n_The Pink Panther_ by Henry Mancini/ arr. J. Krush \n_St. Louis B
 lues_ by W. C. Handy/ arr. G. Pagano \nPiece for Low Brass\, Mvt. IV by S
 teven Franklin\n\nJonathan Randazzo\, trombone\nAmanda Stewart\, trombone\
