SUMMARY:Parent &amp; Family Weekend Wind Ensemble Concert
CLASS:PUBLIC
DESCRIPTION:Cap off your Parent &amp; Family Weekend with a high-energy\,\nfami
 ly-friendly concert you won’t want to miss! Join us for a\n50-minute per
 formance highlighting WashU’s talented student\nmusicians in the Departm
 ent of Music’s largest performing ensembles.\nLed by the powerhouse Wind
  Ensemble and featuring over 65 incredible\nstudents\, this concert promis
 es a toe-tapping celebration of teamwork\,\npassion\, and musical excellen
 ce. After the show\, keep the good vibes\ngoing with a stroll through the 
 Delmar Loop—perfect for a sweet\ntreat or bite to eat before heading hom
 e.\n\nDigital Program\n[https://wustl.box.com/s/jp0w4mnawr07hf0zifvvtepujt
 j30gou]\n\nWatch Live [https://youtube.com/live/OWYfhZwRjU4?feature=share]
 \n\nPROGRAM\n\n_The Fairest of the Fair _by John Philip Sousa\nFirst Suite
  in E-flat for Military Band by Gustav Holst\n_Nocturne _by_ Gabriel Futhe
 y _(member of the WashU Wind Ensemble)\n_Lawrence of Arabia _by_ _Maurice 
 Jarre\, arr. Alfred Reed\n_Play!_ by Carl Holmquist\n
