TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
DTEND;TZID=America/Chicago:20261119T203000
LOCATION:560 Trinity Ave\, University City\, 63130
SUMMARY:WashU Wind Ensemble Concert
CLASS:PUBLIC
DESCRIPTION:Join the WashU Wind Ensemble for an evening of musical contrast
 s\,\ndramatic rhythms\, and cinematic favorites! The program opens with\nR
 obert Sheldon’s _Chiaroscuro_\, exploring the interplay of light and\nda
 rk\, followed by _Nocturne_\, an original work by Wind Ensemble member\nGa
 briel Futhey. John Barnes Chance’s powerful _Incantation and\nDance_ bri
 ngs driving rhythms and intensity to the stage\, while\nMaurice Jarre’s 
 sweeping score from the epic film _Lawrence of\nArabia_\, arranged by Alfr
 ed Reed\, provides a grand cinematic finish.\n\nFree - No tickets or reser
 vations required\n\nDIGITAL PROGRAM\n[https://wustl.box.com/s/jnxuncln44o7
 7d9bw3dzgm00o4sodso6]\n\nWatch Live [https://youtube.com/live/uXW0YMJccJ4?
 feature=share]\n\nPROGRAM\n\nWASHU HORN ENSEMBLE\n_Hansel und Gretel_ by E
 ngelbert Humperdinck\, arr. Jeffry Kirschen\n_Hunter's Chorus _by Carl Mar
 ia von Weber\, arr. Joshua Davis\n\nWASHU PERCUSSION ENSEMBLE\n\"Red Rock 
 Canyon” from _Three Scenes from the Desert_ (2018)  by\nAlex Stopa (b. 
 1980)\n\nWASHU WIND ENSEMBLE\n_Incantation and Dance_ by John Barnes Chanc
 e\n_Nocturne by Gabriel Futhey_ (Member of the WashU Wind Ensemble)\n_Lawr
 ence of Arabia -_ Maurice Jarre\, arr. Alfred Reed\n_Chiaroscuro _by Rober
 t Sheldon\n
