BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:17010
DTSTART;TZID=America/Chicago:20261120T120000
SEQUENCE:0
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
DTEND;TZID=America/Chicago:20261120T130000
SUMMARY:Kemper Unplugged: EcoTones
CLASS:PUBLIC
DESCRIPTION:Curated to intersect with the themes of the Kemper Art Museum
 ’s Fall\n2026 exhibition _Carolina Ceycedo: Growing Deep Roots\, _EcoTon
 es\npresents a concert of chamber jazz works inspired by St. Louis urban\n
 prairies\; relationships of interdependence between plants\,\npollinators\
 , and humans\; and the health and wellbeing of St. Louis\nrivers and their
  nonhuman inhabitants. Inspired by Ceycado’s ongoing\nwork to connect hu
 man\, flora\, and fauna\, this EcoTones performance\npromotes an eco-socia
 l worldview of interrelatedness amongst humans\nand the natural world.  C
 oncertgoers are encouraged to visit the\nmuseum’s exhibition before or a
 fter the concert\, and upon exit\,\nconsider the myriad native species of 
 flora and fauna immediately\nsurrounding the museum as beings with agency\
 , requiring time and space\nto develop into a mature and biodiverse local 
 food web\, thriving\namongst a human-made campus environment.\n\nArrive ea
 rly or stay after to grab lunch at the Museum’s Coffee Bar.\nEnjoy ice c
 ream sandwiches from Sugarwitch\, savory deli sandwiches\nfrom Parker’s 
 Table\, and pastries from Colleen’s. Members get 10%\noff your purchase 
 with every visit. Learn more and join here\n[https://www.kemperartmuseum.w
 ashu.edu/membership].\n\nThese 45-minute concerts are free and open to the
  public.\n\nPERFORMERS\n\nMatthew Allison\, flute\nThomas Jostlein\, alpho
 rn &amp; French horn\nTricia Jostlein\, alphorn &amp; French horn\nRobert Fox\, Fr
 ench horn\nJoel Vanderheyden\, saxophone\nJoseph Hendricks\, bassoon\nJody
  Redhage Ferber\, cello\nVince Varvel\, guitar\nBob Deboo\, bass\n\n \n\n
 BIOGRAPHY\n\nEcoTones Concerts are whimsical outdoor performances\, braidi
 ng\nworld-class musicians\, audiences\, and local public nature spaces to\
 ngrow new audiences for live instrumental music and an eco-social\nworldvi
 ew of interrelatedness amongst humans\, flora\, and fauna. Named\n“Best 
 New Concert Series of 2022” by the _Riverfront Times _of St.\nLouis\, Ec
 oTones features instrumentalists and vocalists performing\nrepertoire insp
 ired by the flora and fauna surrounding trailside\nstages\, encouraging mu
 sicians and audiences to listen in a new way and\nto cultivate a sense of 
 belonging within local nature spaces. EcoTones\nConcerts has presented onc
 e-in-a-lifetime performance events in St.\nLouis’s Tower Grove Park\, St
 . Louis’ legendary Bellefontaine\nCemetery Arboretum\, Nyack\, New York
 ’s River Hook Preserve\, and most\nrecently in Manhattan’s Madison Squ
 are Park\, with an upcoming\npermanent audio trail of newly composed chamb
 er music celebrating the\npark’s notable horticultural collections launc
 hing in Fall 2026.\nPlease visit www.ecotonesconcerts.org\n[http://www.eco
 tonesconcerts.org] for information about upcoming live\nperformances.\n\nP
 hoto Credit: Andrea B. Swenson\n\n \n
DTSTAMP:20261119T182346Z
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:17001
DTSTART;TZID=America/Chicago:20260925T120000
SEQUENCE:0
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
DTEND;TZID=America/Chicago:20260925T130000
SUMMARY:Kemper Unplugged: A Journey Through Latin Sounds
CLASS:PUBLIC
DESCRIPTION:A Journey Through Latin Sounds is a concert that features diffe
 rent\ntraditional covers and original songs from Latin America. To this en
 d\,\nEsteban Tonio &amp; Emerson Magaña play different latin genres and\ninst
 ruments. Some of the Latin rhythms that this concert covers are\ncumbia\, 
 huaynos\, cuban son\, bailecitos\, guajira\, and rumba.\nAdditionally\, di
 fferent instruments are played in this concert such as\nCharango\, Colombi
 an Tiple\, and Quena.\n\nArrive early or stay after to grab lunch at the M
 useum’s Coffee Bar.\nEnjoy ice cream sandwiches from Sugarwitch\, savory
  deli sandwiches\nfrom Parker’s Table\, and pastries from Colleen’s. M
 embers get 10%\noff your purchase with every visit. Learn more and join he
 re\n[https://www.kemperartmuseum.washu.edu/membership].\n\nThese 45-minute
  concerts are free and open to the public.\n\nPERFORMERS\n\nEsteban Tonio\
 nEmerson Magaña\n\nBIOGRAPHIES\n\nESTEBAN TONIO\n\nEsteban Tonio is a Lat
 in folk singer-songwriter currently living in\nthe US. Through his lyrics\
 , Esteban writes about personal reflections\non life\, love\, heartbreak\,
  and everyday experiences. As to his music\,\nEsteban plays mainly nylon-s
 tring guitar\, but he also incorporates\nother Latin American instruments\
 , such as the charango and the\nColombian tiple\, in his songs.\nEsteban h
 as been collaborating with other musicians\, including Kent\nRousseau\, Ch
 ris Endicott\, and Julia Hornberger\, among others. These\ncollaborations 
 have allowed him to incorporate the cello\, violin\,\nelectric guitar\, an
 d keyboard into his songs.\n\nEsteban Tonio is one of the co-founders of t
 he Latin American band Los\nChascones Rotos\, who recorded their first pro
 fessional EP in 2017\nthanks to the song Gülu Mapu\, which won first plac
 e in a music\ncontest organized by Casa de la Cultura Anáhuac of the Sant
 iago\nMetropolitan Park (Parquemet).\n\nEMERSON MAGAÑA\n\nEmerson Magaña
  is a gifted vocalist and classically trained guitarist\nfrom Colima\, Mex
 ico\, currently based in Saint Louis\, MO. He is known\nfor his versatilit
 y as a musician\, navigating between different genres\nand Latin styles an
 d collaborating with a diverse range of musicians.\n\nHis vocals are an em
 bodiment of soulful storytelling\, and his guitar\nskills are a testament 
 to years of dedication to his craft. With a\nstage presence that exudes ch
 arisma and charm\, Emerson connects with\nthe audience on a profound level
 . His unique style and musical\nexperience include alternating musical Lat
 in genres such as:\nBossanova\, Bolero\, Salsa\, Cuban\, Trova\, and more!
 \n
DTSTAMP:20261119T182346Z
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:17002
DTSTART;TZID=America/Chicago:20261023T120000
SEQUENCE:0
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
DTEND;TZID=America/Chicago:20261023T130000
SUMMARY:Kemper Unplugged: From Tango to Bossa Nova
CLASS:PUBLIC
DESCRIPTION:Featuring guitarists W. Mark Akin\, Brian Vaccaro\, and Farshid
 \nSoltanshahi\n\nExplore Latin and Latin-inspired music for classical guit
 ar with\nperformances by W. MARK AKIN and guitar duo BRIAN VACCARO AND FAR
 SHID\nSOLTANSHAHI. Akin will perform works by Sergio Assad\, Máximo Diego
 \nPujol\, and Roland Dyens\, while Vaccaro and Soltanshahi will present a\
 nselection of Latin American music featuring Brazilian Bossa Nova and\nSam
 ba\, as well as Cuban Son Cubano. The program includes compositions\nby An
 tônio Carlos Jobim\, Luiz Bonfá\, Francisco Repilado\, and others.\n\nAr
 rive early or stay after to grab lunch at the Museum’s Coffee Bar.\nEnjo
 y ice cream sandwiches from Sugarwitch\, savory deli sandwiches\nfrom Park
 er’s Table\, and pastries from Colleen’s. Members get 10%\noff your pu
 rchase with every visit. Learn more and join here\n[https://www.kemperartm
 useum.washu.edu/membership].\n\nThese 45-minute concerts are free and open
  to the public.\n\nPERFORMERS\n\nW. Mark Akin\nBrian Vaccaro\nFarshid Solt
 anshahi\n\nBIOGRAPHIES\n\nAward-winning classical guitarist W. MARK AKIN i
 s a St. Louis-based\nmusician who has engaged audiences across the country
  with his dynamic\non-stage presence and musicality.\n\nMark has won prize
 s in numerous competitions such as the Wilson Center\nGuitar Competition i
 n Wisconsin\, Beethoven Club Competition in\nMemphis\, the University of A
 rizona's Beeston Competition and Sholin\nCompetition\, and was most recent
 ly selected as a winner of the Artist\nPresentation Society of St. Louis C
 ompetition.\n\nOriginally from Tennessee\, Mark started his guitar studies
  by learning\nto play electric hard rock\, idolizing guitarists such as Er
 ic Johnson\,\nYngwie Malmsteen\, and Eddie Van Halen.  After discovering 
 the\nclassical guitar in high school\, he then decided to study the\ninstr
 ument full-time and subsequently received his bachelor's and\nmaster's deg
 rees in guitar performance from Belmont University in\nNashville\, and the
  University of Arizona in Tucson.  He has performed\nin master classes an
 d taken lessons with some of the greatest\nguitarists in the world\, namel
 y Sergio and Odair Assad\, Manuel\nBarrueco\, David Russell\, Jason Vieaux
 \, Olivier Chassain\, Marcin Dylla\,\nand Adam Holzman.\n\nAn active teach
 er\, Mark has taught innumerable private lessons and\nclasses. In addition
  to being on faculty at Washington University\, he\nworks with the St. Lou
 is Classical Guitar Society’s outreach\neducation initiative entitled Gu
 itar Horizons.\n\n-------------------------\n\nBRIAN VACCARO graduated fro
 m Webster University in St. Louis in 1996\nwith a Bachelor's Degree in Mus
 ic with an emphasis in Jazz Studies. He\ncontinued his education at Southe
 rn Illinois University at\nEdwardsville\, where he earned a Master's Degre
 e in Music in Guitar\nPerformance in 2000. Since completing his studies\, 
 Brian has been\nactive as an educator as well as a performer. He has taugh
 t a variety\nof jazz and general music courses including Jazz History\, Ja
 zz\nEnsemble\, Guitar Ensemble\, Rock History\, Private Guitar Study\, and
 \nnumerous others at Lindenwood University\, Southwestern Illinois\nColleg
 e\, St. Louis Community College\, Grand Center Arts Academy\, and\nSt. Cha
 rles Community College. In 2010\, Brian received the Outstanding\nAdjunct 
 Faculty award from St. Louis Community College at Meramec.\nBrian is now E
 xecutive Director of the 501c3 organization \"St. Louis\nClassical Guitar\
 ".  He has also performed and recorded with many of\nthe top musicians in
  the St. Louis area.  \"Going Through the\nMotions\"\, the debut album by
  the Brian Vaccaro Trio\, was honored to be\nincluded in the \"Notable Rel
 eases of 2011\" list by noted critic and\nauthor W. Royal Stokes. Brian cu
 rrently performs in and around the St.\nLouis area.\n\n-------------------
 ------\n\nWith a style that’s as diverse as it is captivating\, FARSHID\
 nSOLTANSHAHI brings together various musical forms to create a sound\nthat
 ’s both innovative and deeply rooted in tradition. His work\,\ncharacter
 ized by intricate arrangements and impeccable musicianship\,\nshowcases hi
 s ability to transcend musical genres and cultures.\n\nWhile details on aw
 ards and nominations remain as diverse and eclectic\nas his music\, Farshi
 d Etniko’s discography\, including his celebrated\ndebut album _Nightmar
 e in Heaven_\, stands as a testament to his\nartistic brilliance. With top
  songs and albums that feature a rich\ntapestry of sounds—from the class
 ical guitar preludes to the\npowerful fusion of drums\, bass\, and traditi
 onal Persian\ninstruments—Farshid’s music invites listeners into a wor
 ld where\nmusical boundaries cease to exist.\n\n \n
DTSTAMP:20261119T182346Z
END:VEVENT
