CLASS:PUBLIC
DESCRIPTION:Get ready for an afternoon of movie magic\, musical adventures\
 , and a\nlittle bit of everything in between! The WashU Symphony Orchestra
 \npresents \"Capes\, Chocolate and Cartoons\,\" a fun-filled concert\nfeat
 uring music from some of your favorite movies\, musicals\, and\nanimated h
 its! From the heroic sounds of _Superman_ and _Star Wars_ to\nthe whimsica
 l worlds of _Willy Wonka_\, _Encanto_\, and _Aladdin_\,\nthere's something
  for everyone. Throw in T_he Polar Express\,\nHamilton_\, and even _K-Pop 
 Demon Hunters_\, and you've got a musical\nadventure the whole family will
  love!\n\nFree - No tickets or reservations required\n\nDIGITAL PROGRAM\n[
 https://wustl.box.com/s/y7t52ireedye4n7v7fchcfx4lv9nlv64]\n\nWatch Live [h
 ttps://youtube.com/live/g2Y-fORysNA?feature=share]\n\nPROGRAM\n\n_Superman
  Returns _(2006) by John Williams &amp; John Ottman (b. 1964)\n_Pure Imaginat
 ion _from_ WONKA _(2023) by Leslie Bricusse &amp; Anthony\nNewley (1931 – 2
 021\, 1931 – 1999)\n_Aladdin _(1992) by Alan Menken &amp; Tim Rice (b. 1949
 \, b. 1944)\n_Suite _from_ Hamilton _(2015) by Lin-Manuel Miranda (b. 19
 80)\n_Selections _from_ Encanto _(2021) by Lin-Manuel Miranda \n_Selecti
 ons _from_ The Polar Express_ (2004) by Glen Ballard &amp; Alan\nSilvestri (b.
  1953\, b. 1950)\n_The Empire Strikes Back Medley _(1980) by John William
 s (b. 1932)\n_K-Pop Demon Hunters Medley _(2025) arr. Daryl McKenzie (b. 
 1962)\n
DTSTAMP:20261119T182346Z
END:VEVENT
