SUMMARY:WashU Symphony Orchestra Concert: “Tapestry of Sounds” featurin
 g\npianist Nina Ferrigno
CLASS:PUBLIC
DESCRIPTION:“Tapestry of Sounds\,” featuring WashU faculty pianist Nina
 \nFerrigno\, brings together drama\, virtuosity\, and brilliant orchestral
 \ncolor. The WashU Symphony Orchestra and conductor Darwin Aquino move\nfr
 om the operatic excitement of Verdi’s _Nabucco_ Overture to\nGrieg’s d
 azzling Piano Concerto in A minor\, followed by the St.\nLouis premiere of
  Armando Bayolo’s _A Shelter that Filters the Sun_.\nThe evening wraps u
 p with Britten’s lively _Soirées Musicales_—a\ncolorful finale filled
  with dance\, energy\, and orchestral sparkle.\n\nDigital Program\n[https:
 //wustl.box.com/s/nbz0lo88u81nral1vtgj3x67yuklhvzl]\n\nWatch Live [https:/
 /youtube.com/live/_DCShB0tDN4?feature=share]\n\nPROGRAM\n\nOverture to _Na
 bucco_ by Giuseppe Verdi \n \nPiano Concerto in A minor Op. 16 by Edvard
  Grieg \n     I. _Allegro molto moderato_\n     II. _Adagio_\n   
   III. _Allegro moderato molto e marcato_\nNina Ferrigno\, piano\n \nInt
 ermission \n \n_A Shelter that Filters the Sun_ (STL premiere) by Armand
 o Bayolo \n \n_Soirées Musicales\, _Op. 9 by Benjamin Britten\n     
 I. _March_\n     II. _Canzonetta_\n     III. _Tirolese_\n     IV.
  _Bolero_\n     V. _Tarantella _
DTSTAMP:20261119T182346Z
END:VEVENT
