BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:16874
DTSTART;TZID=America/Chicago:20251206T193000
SEQUENCE:0
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
DTEND;TZID=America/Chicago:20251206T203000
LOCATION:560 Trinity Ave\, University City\, 63130
SUMMARY:Holiday Celebrations: Lights\, Laughter\, and Fa-La-La
CLASS:PUBLIC
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a magical evening at \"Holiday Celebrations: Lights
 \,\nLaughter\, and Fa-La-La\" in the E. Desmond Lee Concert Hall\, located
 \nwithin the 560 Music Center. Revel in the holiday spirit as the WashU\nJ
 azz Band\, Concert and Chamber Choirs\, and jazz combo program present\na 
 diverse selection of music that spans the genres and eras\, all with\na sp
 ecial seasonal twist. From classic holiday tunes to contemporary\nfavorite
 s\, there’s something for everyone to enjoy. Don’t miss\nthis opportun
 ity to celebrate with music\, merriment\, and community!\nJoin us for the 
 Department of Music Holiday Party following the\nconcert with performances
  by the WashU Jazz Combos! Drinks and dessert\nwill be provided.\n\nFREE\,
  family-friendly\n\nPROGRAM\n\nJAZZ BAND\n\n_Strike Up the Band_ (1940) Mu
 sic and Lyrics by George Gershwin and\nIra Gershwin\, Arranged by Mark Tay
 lor\n\n_Have Yourself a Merry Little Christmas_ (1943) from the film _Meet
  Me\nin St. Louis _Words and Music by Hugh Martin (1914-2011) and Ralph\nB
 lane (1914-1995)\, Arranged by Alan Baylock (in the style of Neal\nHefti's
  _Lil' Darlin'_)\n\nWASHU CONCERT CHOIR\n\n_Deck the Hall_ (1958) Traditio
 nal Welsh Carol\, Arranged by Alice\nParker (1925-2023)\n\n_Bashana Haba
 ’ah_ (1994) Lyrics by Ehud Manor (1941-2005)\, Music by\nNurit Hirsch (b
 . 1942)\, Arranged by John Leavitt (b. 1956)\n     Felix Guo\, clarinet
 \, Claire Yi\, violin\, Evelyn Nedelciuc\,\ncello\, Melissa Parkinson\, do
 uble bass\, and Yeon-Kyung Kim\, piano\n\n     Translation: Next year\,
  when peace will come\, we shall return\nto the simple pleasures of life s
 o long denied us. You will see\, you\nwill see\, O how good it will be\, n
 ext year!\n\nSING-ALONG\n\n _Jingle Bells_ \n\nSOLOS/DUETS\n\n_Let It Sn
 ow! Let It Snow! Let It Snow! _by_ _Sammy Cahn and Jule\nStyne\n     Ph
 il Zhang and Vincent Varvel\, guitars\n\n_The Christmas Song_ arr. by Jaco
 b Koller\n     Hayden McAlister\, jazz piano\n\nJAZZ BAND\n\n_My Funny 
 Valentine_ (1937) from _Babes in Arms _Words by Lorenz Hart\n(1895-1943)\,
  Music by Richard Rodgers (1902-1979)\, Arranged by Sammy\nNestico\n_Winte
 r Wonderland_ (1934) Words by Dick Smith (1901-1935)\, Music by\nFelix Ber
 nard (1897-1944)\, Arranged by Dave Wolpe\n\nCHAMBER CHOIR\n\n_Bell Carol_
  (2014) Traditional Ukrainian Carol Arranged with Original\nWords by Heath
 er Sorenson  \n     Young Whun Kim and Yeon-Kyung Kim\, piano\n\nJAZZ 
 BAND\n\n_Salsa Amigo_ (1982) Composed and Arranged by Pete Coulman (1956-2
 016)\n\nJAZZ BAND AND CHAMBER CHOIR\n\n_Rudolph\, the Red-Nosed Reindeer_ 
 (2022) Words and Music by Johnny\nMarks\, Additional Lyrics by Garry Willi
 ams\, Arranged by Garry Williams\nand Alvin Trotman\n\n \n
DTSTAMP:20261119T182346Z
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:16912
DTSTART;TZID=America/Chicago:20260317T193000
SEQUENCE:0
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
DTEND;TZID=America/Chicago:20260317T203000
LOCATION:560 Trinity Ave\, University City\, 63130
SUMMARY:WashU Jazz Series: William Lenihan\, Paul DeMarinis Quartet
CLASS:PUBLIC
DESCRIPTION:The William Lenihan/Paul DeMarinis Group will perform original 
 music -\nand music of John McLaughlin\, Ralph Towner. The evening features
  music\nof the instrumental group - with featured cameo vocal performances
  of\nsinger Chloe Haynes\, including music from McLaughlin's _Apocalypse_.
 \n\nThroughout the semester\, enjoy free live performances by noted local\
 nand regional jazz artists at the 560 Music Center!\n\nMUSICIANS\n\nPaul 
 DeMarinis\, saxophones\nWilliam Lenihan\, guitar\, piano\nRic Vice\, bass\
 nKyle Honeycutt\, drums\nZach Radwine\, piano\nChloe Haynes\, voice\n\nWIL
 LIAM LENIHAN\n\nWilliam Lenihan is a composer\, guitarist\, and pianist wo
 rking in the\nfields of new music\, jazz\, classical music\, and film musi
 c. In the\njazz world\, he has performed or recorded with Ron Carter\, Mic
 hael\nBrecker\, Dave Weckl\, Marc Copland\, John Patitucci\, Gary Husband\
 , Bob\nBrookmeyer\, George Lewis\, and many others. As well\, he works in\
 norchestral and chamber music as a classical guitarist. His work in\ntheat
 rical music includes that with icons from the Broadway music and\nHollywoo
 d film worlds. \n\nAs a composer\, he is regularly commissioned for work 
 in chamber music\,\nhis works having been recorded by members of the St. L
 ouis Symphony\nOrchestra\, as well as soloists and chamber ensembles in Eu
 rope. His\nmost recent collaboration includes a large-scale work with Ital
 ian\nflutist\, Roberto Fabbriciani. His newest recording\, _The Reprieve_\
 nwith Weckl/Husband/Patitucci\, will be released in spring 2026. His\nprim
 ary teachers include Ralph Towner\, Richie Beirach\, and Gary\nPeacock.  
 \n\nPAUL DEMARINIS\n\nSaxophonist Paul DeMarinis and guitarist William Len
 ihan\, longtime\nmusical associates\, perform their newest music with a co
 mpelling new\nensemble. Over decades\, their collaborations have been nume
 rous\, with\nconcerts encompassing small groups to big bands. Demarinis ha
 s\nperformed with many artists\, including Dave Liebman\, Ray Charles\,\nC
 ount Basie Orchestra. Lenihan has performed with Ron Carter\, Bob\nBrookme
 yer\, Gary Husband\, and Dave Weckl\, among numerous others.\nTogether\, t
 hey bring a fresh voice to new music in song and\nimprovisation.\n
DTSTAMP:20261119T182346Z
END:VEVENT
