DESCRIPTION:Arrive early or stay after to grab lunch at the Museum’s Coff
 ee Bar.\nEnjoy ice cream sandwiches from Sugarwitch\, savory deli sandwich
 es\nfrom Parker’s Table\, and pastries from Colleen’s. Members get 10%
 \noff your purchase with every visit. Learn more and join here\n[https://w
 ww.kemperartmuseum.washu.edu/membership].\n\nThese 45-minute concerts are 
 free and open to the public.\n\nTHE MUSICIANS\n\nMark Tonelli - guitar\nFe
 yza Eren - vocals\nBennett Wood - saxophone and flute\nBen Wheeler - bass\
 nBen Dicke - drums\n\nABOUT\n\nMARK TONELLI AND AFOLIA \n\nDiscover the s
 oulful sounds of Brazil with Mark Tonelli &amp; Afolia! This\nunique group of 
 top St. Louis musicians shines a spotlight on\nlesser-known Brazilian gems
 \, moving beyond the classic bossa novas to\nunearth hidden treasures. Joi
 n Afolia as they take you on a journey\nthrough the vibrant rhythms and po
 ignant melodies of 1970’s and\n80’s Brazil\, celebrating the richness 
 of Brazilian music. Afolia has\nperformed in renowned St. Louis venues suc
 h as The Dark Room and Blue\nStrawberry and has appeared on CBS KMOVTV Cha
 nnel 4’s Emmy-nominated\n“The Stage.”\n\n \n\n \n
